+// requireDeviceBoundToAccessPoint guards RecordEvent/SettleTripCash/
+// CancelBoardingTrip/RecordWalkOnCashEntry — the four access_points
+// operations the device gateway (cmd/api/main.go's apiGatewayGroup, master
+// plan §9 madde 1) reaches by AccessPoint id — against a device operating on
+// an AccessPoint it is not configured for. Must run, and must return nil,
+// before any of those four does anything with a financial, ledger or
+// trip-state side effect.
+//
+// callerIsAPIClient and apiClientID come from the handler's own gin.Context
+// ("user_type"/"userID", set only by APIClientAuthRequired from the verified
+// token — never from the request body or query). A human admin
+// (callerIsAPIClient=false) is unaffected: DeviceBindings has no meaning for
+// them, and their own permission/role gating already applies unchanged.
+//
+// Tenant/site scoping is handled earlier, by the FindByID query that
+// produced ap (tenantfilter) — an AccessPoint outside the caller's own
+// tenant/site cannot be found at all, so ap here is already confirmed to be
+// in-scope. This is the finer check on top: being in the same tenant/site is
+// not, by itself, enough.
